Transfer Regeneration (Transmutation)
Saves: None	DC: 	Casting: 1 standard action
Duration: 1 minute	Range: Close (35 ft.)	Components: V,S
SR: No	Effect: You bestow your regenerative abilities on the target. Your regeneration stops functioning for the duration of the spell, and the target gains your regeneration. For example, if you have regeneration 5 [acid or fire], your target gains regeneration 5 [acid or fire]. This regeneration overlaps [does not stack] with any regeneration the creature already has, including other castings of this spell. This spell has no effect if you don't have the regeneration ability or your regeneration isn't functioning when you cast the spell.	Target: 1 willing living creature
DESC: You bestow your regenerative abilities on the target. Your regeneration stops functioning for the duration of the spell, and the target gains your regeneration. For example, if you have regeneration 5 (acid or fire), your target gains regeneration 5 (acid or fire). This regeneration overlaps (does not stack) with any regeneration the creature already has, including other castings of this spell. This spell has no effect if you don't have the regeneration ability or your regeneration isn't functioning when you cast the spell.
DESC 2:  You bestow your regenerative abilities on the target. Your regeneration stops functioning for the duration of the spell, and the target gains your regeneration. For example, if you have regeneration 5 [acid or fire], your target gains regeneration 5 [acid or fire]. This regeneration overlaps [does not stack] with any regeneration the creature already has, including other castings of this spell. This spell has no effect if you don't have the regeneration ability or your regeneration isn't functioning when you cast the spell.
Trial by Fire (Evocation)
Saves: None	DC: 	Casting: 1 standard action
Duration: Instantaneous	Range: Touch	Components: V,S,DF
SR: Yes	Effect: You test a creature's purity of convictions by exposing it to a sheet of divine fire. Unless the target's alignment is within one step of your deity's, the spell deals 2d6 points of damage. Half the damage is fire damage, but the other half results directly from divine power and is therefore not subject to being reduced by resistance to fire-based attacks. Additionally, if the target has an element of its alignment that is in direct opposition to your deity's [chaos opposes law and evil opposes good], you can also attempt an Intimidate check to demoralize the target as a free action.	Target: Creature touched
DESC: You test a creature's purity of convictions by exposing it to a sheet of divine fire. Unless the target's alignment is within one step of your deity's, the spell deals (min(5,CASTERLEVEL/2))d6 points of damage. Half the damage is fire damage, but the other half results directly from divine power and is therefore not subject to being reduced by resistance to fire-based attacks. Additionally, if the target has an element of its alignment that is in direct opposition to your deity's (chaos opposes law and evil opposes good), you can also attempt an Intimidate check to demoralize the target as a free action.
DESC 2:  You test a creature's purity of convictions by exposing it to a sheet of divine fire. Unless the target's alignment is within one step of your deity's, the spell deals 2d6 points of damage. Half the damage is fire damage, but the other half results directly from divine power and is therefore not subject to being reduced by resistance to fire-based attacks. Additionally, if the target has an element of its alignment that is in direct opposition to your deity's [chaos opposes law and evil opposes good], you can also attempt an Intimidate check to demoralize the target as a free action.
Trial of Fire and Acid (Evocation)
Saves: Fortitude half (see text)	DC: 17	Casting: 1 standard action
Duration: 5 rounds	Range: Touch	Components: V,S
SR: No	Effect: The target creature is covered in burning acid that deals 1d6 points of acid damage and 1d6 points of fire damage each round. The subject can attempt a Fortitude saving throw each round to reduce the damage by half. Dousing the target in water ends the effect [both the acid and the fire], but rolling on the ground does not extinguish the fire or affect the acid.	Target: Creature touched
DESC: The target creature is covered in burning acid that deals 1d6 points of acid damage and 1d6 points of fire damage each round. The subject can attempt a Fortitude saving throw each round to reduce the damage by half. Dousing the target in water ends the effect (both the acid and the fire), but rolling on the ground does not extinguish the fire or affect the acid.
DESC 2:  The target creature is covered in burning acid that deals 1d6 points of acid damage and 1d6 points of fire damage each round. The subject can attempt a Fortitude saving throw each round to reduce the damage by half. Dousing the target in water ends the effect [both the acid and the fire], but rolling on the ground does not extinguish the fire or affect the acid.
